Z||000003||Old Lar||02-02-2001||04:49 PM||||Any auto finisher supply house can mix up the color for interior paint.  If you tell them the year and color they can match it.  I've been retouching miscellaneous plastic interior parts with a small air brush sprayer and it works real good.  I've had a pint of the interior mix for several years.  keep the can close when not in use.||||reg||3
Z||000004||CHARLIE FERGUSON||02-02-2001||05:20 PM||||THE GREY PART THAT I AM TALKING ABOUT IS THE LIGHT GREY LOWER PART OF THE DASH AROUND THE VENTS. LT. GREY IS VERY HARD TO MATCH, USED A PREVEL SRAYER W/VINYL DYE BEFORE, BUT ON THE FIERO I DONT HAVE MUCH ROOM FOR ERRORS.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||02-02-2001||07:07 PM||||umm, I'd like to make a little suggestion, turn off the caps lock. Everyone here translates that as yelling.<P>the dash is extremely easy to remove from the car, then you can take out the vent pieces and spray away. I swapped my 85GT dash out with an 86GT dash in about 1 1/2 hours, it only took that long because I also added the wiring harness for power mirrors.<P>Good Luck.||||reg||1
